        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Menindee Lakes, Menindee, New South Wales, Menindee County, Australia\n- Organizations: Central Darling Shire\n- Concepts: location, population, spelling\n\nFacts:\n- Menindee is a small town in the far west of New South Wales, Australia.\n- Menindee is in Central Darling Shire and on the banks of the Darling River.\n- Menindee is frequently but erroneously spelled \"Menindie\".\n- The 2011 census recorded Menindee with a population of 449.\n- A sign in Menindee states a population of 980.\n- Menindee Lakes lie in the far west region of New South Wales, Australia, near the town of Menindee.\n- Menindee Lakes are located in Menindee County.",
